# Suggested .gitignore for a markdown vault (Obsidian, Foam, …) managed by claudesidion.
# Copy to the root of your vault. The push hook also refuses secret-shaped filenames, but a
# blocklist can never be complete — this is the durable half of that guard.

# Obsidian's own per-machine state (workspace layout, cache). Keep your settings if you
# sync them deliberately; drop the whole folder if you do not.
/.obsidian/workspace*
/.obsidian/cache
/.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# VS Code / Foam per-machine state. Settings and recommended extensions are what make the vault
# open the same everywhere, so they stay tracked; Foam's templates live in .foam/ and stay too.
/.vscode/*
!/.vscode/settings.json
!/.vscode/extensions.json

# Secrets and credentials — never in a synced knowledge base.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.crt
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
.npmrc
.netrc
.pgpass
credentials

# OS and editor noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp

# Scratch space. Anything here is yours to manage; the plugin will not commit it.
/Scratch/
/tmp/
